From a2d1f9c9a54eaf535e24c312d681599db602c7ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EmberGate <jebadiahgreenwood@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:25:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] llama : optional <arch>.layer_schedule for synthetic layer
 repeats (EmberGate R5/S1, on b11901)

Squash of the two master commits (r5-master 46ecaf09 + b2bbbd5c) re-applied on b11901 (5320c87f),
for Ollama v0.40.12's llama/compat/002-embergate-layer-schedule.patch. Applied without conflict
(only line offsets differ from the master version).

A GGUF may carry <arch>.layer_schedule, an array of FILE trunk layer indices, one per trunk
POSITION (e.g. B1 on a 32-layer Qwen3.5 = 0..7, 4..7, 8..31 = 36 positions). The trunk runs
those layers in that order with the weights shared; every per-layer hparams array and dev_layer is
re-indexed by position so each position has its own cache slot (KV / conv + recurrent state).
MTP/NextN layers keep their file names and sit after the trunk. Refused (with the reason) when
n_layer_decision > 0, and deepseek41's layer-reference arrays are remapped only for that arch.
No key: no change.
